2 CONT NST XX1 s 244: Asgaut Steinnes: Om dei eldste norske drikkehorni: mor?
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Kilde: http://www.valeforlag.no/images/pdf/VFSKap1.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Story: Before the Reformation 1536 Norway was a catholic country and the biggest landowner was the Catholic church. People who could afford it gave a part of a farm or an entire farm to the church as a "gift" just to be mentioned 
2 CONC by name and bede for the soul in the first servant of God after their own funeral.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shortly before 1400. Gift from Erlend Filippusson Losna to Nidaros (Trondheim) bishopric./Catholic priest- and bishophud.  He gives the whole farm Gjemmestad in Gloppen, Nordfjord, the value of 20 "Månedsmatsmål" (Adequate value i
2 CONC n butter and grain to feed a man in 20 months) Erlend Losna died 1407, link
2 CONT
2 CONT After the reformation the king took all the farms.
